---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import OptionsTable from "../components/api/OptionsTable.astro";
import PropertiesTable from "../components/api/PropertiesTable.astro";
import InstanceNote from "../components/api/InstanceNote.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "introduction", label: "Introduction", heading: false },
  { id: "initialization", label: "Initialization" },
  { id: "options", label: "Options" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Methods" },
  { id: "properties", label: "Properties" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="autocomplete" sections={S}>
<p>Autocomplete keeps the original suggestion dataset and the selected display label while the user edits. Escape and Tab in the input close the menu and cancel a pending open. Listbox options stay out of the sequential Tab order.</p>
<p><code>isOpen</code> follows the suggestion menu through rerenders and dismissal. When the selection changes, the input emits a bubbling, composed <code>change</code> event, so delegated form listeners can observe it.</p>

  <p>Autocomplete adds a visually hidden, polite live region for loading, result counts and multi-selection changes. The visible spinner and count stay unchanged. It announces only while the input has focus and its text meets <code>minLength</code>. Closing the menu clears the region. Check spoken delivery with a screen reader.</p>
  <p>Override <code>i18n.loading</code> and <code>i18n.noResults</code>, which default to "Loading results." and "No results.". For localized plurals, supply <code>i18n.results(count)</code> and <code>i18n.selected(count)</code> functions. The defaults produce "1 result available." or "N results available." and "1 item selected." or "N items selected.". <code>i18n.create(text)</code> labels the "Add" row and defaults to <code>Add "text"</code>. Missing keys keep their defaults. All messages are plain text.</p>
  <p>When a search returns no suggestions, the open list also shows <code>i18n.noResults</code> as its first row, so sighted users see what the live region says. The row is not an option. It is hidden from assistive technology, arrow keys skip it, and a click on it chooses nothing and leaves focus in the field. The row goes away when a search returns a match. In Chips, pressing Enter to add the typed text as a chip closes the list.</p>
  <p>Updates announce the count passed to <code>setMenuItems</code>, excluding fallback selected items, disabled entries and the "Add" row. Opening an existing list announces its displayed item count, without disabled entries. Updates with <code>open: false</code> stay silent. Your application handles request cancellation, stale-response ordering and errors. The plugin ignores results delivered after <code>destroy()</code>, and results delivered after the user leaves the field update the list without opening it.</p>
  <Section {...S.introduction}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          Add <code>autocomplete</code> to a text input inside <code>.field</code>.
          <code>AutoInit()</code> starts every <code>.autocomplete</code> except
          those with <code>no-autoinit</code>. The default <code>data</code> list is empty,
          so pass options, or call <code>init</code>, to give it something to suggest.
        </p>
        <div class="field mb-5">
          <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">textsms</span>
          <input type="text" id="autocomplete-input" class="autocomplete no-autoinit" placeholder=" ">
          <label for="autocomplete-input">Autocomplete</label>
        </div>
        <p>Set <code>isMultiSelect: true</code> to pick several values. A count appears on the field.</p>
        <div class="field mb-5">
          <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">textsms</span>
          <input type="text" id="autocomplete-multi" class="autocomplete no-autoinit" placeholder=" ">
          <label for="autocomplete-multi">Multiple Autocomplete</label>
        </div>
        <p>Set <code>disabled: true</code> on an entry to show it without letting anyone choose it. Oslo is unavailable, and Vienna is selected and cannot be removed.</p>
        <div class="field mb-5">
          <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">location_city</span>
          <input type="text" id="autocomplete-disabled" class="autocomplete no-autoinit" placeholder=" ">
          <label for="autocomplete-disabled">Cities</label>
        </div>
        <p>Set <code>group</code> on entries to list them under headings.</p>
        <div class="field mb-5">
          <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">public</span>
          <input type="text" id="autocomplete-groups" class="autocomplete no-autoinit" placeholder=" ">
          <label for="autocomplete-groups">Grouped cities</label>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="field">
  <span class="material-symbols prefix" aria-hidden="true">textsms</span>
  <input type="text" id="autocomplete-input" class="autocomplete" placeholder=" ">
  <label for="autocomplete-input">Autocomplete</label>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>

  <Section {...S.initialization}>
        <p>
          The IIFE bundle exposes <code>Expressive.Autocomplete</code>.
          <code>data</code> is an array of objects:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>id</strong> (required). A string or number, used as the option text
            when <code>text</code> is omitted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>text</strong>. The display label. The default search matches
            <code>id</code> and <code>text</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>image</strong>. An image URL, shown as a circle. The default search ignores it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>description</strong>. An optional secondary line under the label.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>disabled</strong>. <code>true</code> keeps the entry in the list,
            dimmed, but nobody can choose it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>group</strong>. An optional heading to list the entry under.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The default search ignores extra properties. Filter them yourself in
          <code>onSearch</code>.
        </p>
<Code code={`
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
  const elems = document.querySelectorAll('.autocomplete');
  Expressive.Autocomplete.init(elems, {
    minLength: 0,
    data: [
      { id: 12, text: 'Apple' },
      { id: 13, text: 'Microsoft' },
      { id: 42, text: 'Google', image: 'https://picsum.photos/id/64/250/250' }
    ]
  });
});
`} />
        <p>Multiple selection:</p>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Autocomplete.init(document.querySelector('#autocomplete-multi'), {
  minLength: 0,
  isMultiSelect: true,
  data: [
    { id: 12, text: 'Apple' },
    { id: 13, text: 'Microsoft' },
    { id: 42, text: 'Google', image: 'https://picsum.photos/id/64/250/250' }
  ]
});
`} />
        <p>
          A disabled entry stays in the results so people can see it exists.
          A click, Enter and <code>selectOption()</code> all leave it as it is,
          so no <code>change</code> or <code>expressive:autocomplete</code> fires.
          Up and Down skip it, and the announced result count leaves it out,
          so a list of only disabled matches announces <code>i18n.noResults</code>.
          The <code>selected</code> option and <code>setMenuItems(items, selected)</code>
          can still select one, which shows a choice the person cannot remove:
        </p>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Autocomplete.init(document.querySelector('#autocomplete-disabled'), {
  minLength: 0,
  isMultiSelect: true,
  selected: ['vienna'],
  data: [
    { id: 'lisbon', text: 'Lisbon' },
    { id: 'oslo', text: 'Oslo', disabled: true },
    { id: 'rome', text: 'Rome' },
    { id: 'vienna', text: 'Vienna', disabled: true }
  ]
});
`} />
        <p>
          Give entries a <code>group</code> to list them under labelled headings. Entries with the same group gather where the group first appears in the results, so sort them yourself if the order matters; entries without one stay outside every group. Up and Down pass over a heading to the next entry, the announced result count leaves headings out, and a click on a heading chooses nothing. The heading is plain text, even with <code>allowUnsafeHTML</code>:
        </p>
<Code code={`
Expressive.Autocomplete.init(document.querySelector('#autocomplete-groups'), {
  minLength: 0,
  data: [
    { id: 'lisbon', text: 'Lisbon', group: 'Portugal' },
    { id: 'porto', text: 'Porto', group: 'Portugal' },
    { id: 'bergen', text: 'Bergen', group: 'Norway' },
    { id: 'oslo', text: 'Oslo', group: 'Norway' }
  ]
});
`} />
        <p>
          A custom <code>onSearch</code> can load data asynchronously. When the list is
          ready, call <code>setMenuItems</code>. The default filter looks at
          <code>id</code> and <code>text</code> only:
        </p>
<Code code={`
onSearch: function(text, autocomplete) {
  const normSearch = text.toLocaleLowerCase();
  autocomplete.setMenuItems(
    autocomplete.options.data.filter(function(option) {
      return option.id.toString().toLocaleLowerCase().includes(normSearch)
        || (option.text && option.text.toLocaleLowerCase().includes(normSearch));
    })
  );
}
`} />
        <p>
          The third argument is an <code>AbortSignal</code>. It aborts when the
          search text changes or the autocomplete is destroyed. Pass it to
          <code>fetch()</code> so a slow response for old text never replaces
          the results for the current text. Clear the list on any other
          error. Set <code>searchDelay</code> so the request waits for typing
          to pause instead of going out on every key:
        </p>
<Code code={`
searchDelay: 300,
onSearch: function(text, autocomplete, signal) {
  fetch('/api/search?q=' + encodeURIComponent(text), { signal })
    .then(function(response) { return response.json(); })
    .then(function(items) { autocomplete.setMenuItems(items); })
    .catch(function(error) {
      // A newer search aborted this one; its results are stale.
      if (error.name !== 'AbortError') autocomplete.setMenuItems([]);
    });
}
`} />
        <p>
          Set <code>allowCreate</code> to offer the typed text as a new value.
          The list then ends in an "Add" row whenever the trimmed text matches
          no listed suggestion. The comparison ignores case and checks each
          suggestion's <code>text</code>, or its <code>id</code> when it has no
          <code>text</code>. Choosing the row with Enter or a click calls
          <code>onCreate</code> with the trimmed text and fires
          <code>expressive:create</code> with <code>&#123; text &#125;</code>.
          The selection does not change, so add and select the entry yourself:
        </p>
<Code code={`
allowCreate: true,
onCreate: function(text, autocomplete) {
  const entry = { id: text, text: text };
  autocomplete.options.data.push(entry);
  autocomplete.setMenuItems(autocomplete.options.data, [entry.id], false);
}
`} />
  </Section>

  <Section {...S.options}>
        <OptionsTable>
            <tr>
              <td><code>data</code></td>
              <td>Array</td>
              <td><code>[]</code></td>
              <td>Suggestion list. Each item needs an <code>id</code>. The <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, and <code>description</code> fields are optional.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>isMultiSelect</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td><code>false</code></td>
              <td>If true, the user can select several values. <code>onAutocomplete</code> receives an array.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>maxMenuHeight</code></td>
              <td>String</td>
              <td><code>'300px'</code></td>
              <td>Max height of the suggestion menu.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>onAutocomplete</code></td>
              <td>Function</td>
              <td><code>null</code></td>
              <td>Called after a selection and when a default value is applied. Receives the selected entries.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>onSearch</code></td>
              <td>Function</td>
              <td>filters <code>id</code> and <code>text</code></td>
              <td>Called with the text, the instance and an <code>AbortSignal</code> when input events change the search text, including paste, replacement and deletion without key events. Load or filter data, then call <code>setMenuItems</code>. The signal aborts when the search text changes or the autocomplete is destroyed.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>allowCreate</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td><code>false</code></td>
              <td>If true, text that matches no listed suggestion exactly ends the list in an "Add" row. Choosing it calls <code>onCreate</code> and fires <code>expressive:create</code>. The selection does not change.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>onCreate</code></td>
              <td>Function</td>
              <td><code>null</code></td>
              <td>Called with the trimmed text and the instance when the "Add" row is chosen.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>searchDelay</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>0</code></td>
              <td>Milliseconds to wait after typing pauses before calling <code>onSearch</code>, so remote data is fetched once per pause. A search on focus runs at once. Blur, <code>destroy()</code> and choosing a single result cancel a pending search. <code>0</code> searches on every input.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>minLength</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td><code>1</code></td>
              <td>Characters required before suggestions open. <code>0</code> shows the list on click or focus.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>menuOptions</code></td>
              <td>Object</td>
              <td>see note</td>
              <td>
                Options for
                <a href={`${route('menu')}#options`}>Menu</a>.
                Defaults include <code>autoFocus: false</code>,
                <code>closeOnClick: false</code>, and <code>coverTrigger: false</code>.
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>allowUnsafeHTML</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td><code>false</code></td>
              <td>If true, each data entry's <code>text</code> is inserted as HTML. Ids always stay text. Only use sanitized data.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>selected</code></td>
              <td>Array</td>
              <td><code>[]</code></td>
              <td>Initial selected ids (strings or numbers). An id without loaded data displays the id. Pass the selected ids to <code>setMenuItems</code> with the loaded data to resolve their labels.</td>
            </tr>
        </OptionsTable>
  </Section>

  <Section {...S.methods}>
        <InstanceNote plugin="Autocomplete" />

        <h5 class="light">.open();</h5>
        <p>Open the suggestion menu if the input meets <code>minLength</code>.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.open();
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.close();</h5>
        <p>Close the suggestion menu.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.close();
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.selectOption();</h5>
        <p>Select (or toggle, when multi-select) the entry with this id.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.selectOption(42);
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.setMenuItems();</h5>
        <p>Replace the visible suggestions. Optionally pass selected ids and whether to open the menu (default <code>true</code>).</p>
<Code code={`
instance.setMenuItems([
  { id: 'Test' },
  { id: 12, text: 'Apple' },
  { id: 13, text: 'Microsoft' },
  { id: 42, text: 'Google', image: 'https://picsum.photos/id/64/250/250' }
]);
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.destroy();</h5>
        <p>Destroy the plugin instance, remove the menu, and detach its event handlers.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.destroy();
`} />
  </Section>

  <Section {...S.properties}>
        <PropertiesTable el="The input the plugin was initialized with.">
            <tr>
              <td><code>isOpen</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td>Whether the suggestion menu is open.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>count</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td>Number of matching options (reset on each input or focus).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>activeIndex</code></td>
              <td>Number</td>
              <td>Index of the keyboard-highlighted option, or <code>-1</code>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>menu</code></td>
              <td>Menu</td>
              <td>The Menu instance for this autocomplete.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>selectedValues</code></td>
              <td>Array</td>
              <td>The currently selected entries.</td>
            </tr>
        </PropertiesTable>
  </Section>

</DocsLayout>
